209
00:14:50,383 --> 00:14:53,599
Read the question on screen.
Say your answer out loud.

210
00:14:58,439 --> 00:15:02,244
A strong answer is about timing
and about who does the evaluating.

211
00:15:02,284 --> 00:15:07,021
For the first form: what evaluates the
expression, where the result goes, and what

212
00:15:07,061 --> 00:15:11,856
the shell then parses. For the second: what
is evaluated by Actions, what the shell

213
00:15:11,896 --> 00:15:16,109
parses, and at which moment the value
reaches the shell and in what role.

214
00:15:16,449 --> 00:15:21,358
It ends with the consequence for review.
The follow-up is about gating a step on

215
00:15:21,398 --> 00:15:25,441
whether a secret is set with an if
that reads the secrets context.

216
00:15:25,481 --> 00:15:30,514
Recall from video 143 which contexts an if
can read and what timing has to do with

217
00:15:30,554 --> 00:15:30,700
it.

218
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:33,467
Let's land this.

219
00:15:33,807 --> 00:15:35,467
You should now be able to say:

220
00:15:35,807 --> 00:15:40,795
An expression inside run is pasted into the
script text before the shell starts: it

221
00:15:40,835 --> 00:15:41,704
generates code.

222
00:15:42,044 --> 00:15:47,670
Titles, bodies, labels, branch names,
commit messages, author names and addresses

223
00:15:47,710 --> 00:15:49,769
are text an outsider controls.

224
00:15:50,109 --> 00:15:54,566
Through env the script is a constant, and
the value arrives as data in a variable

225
00:15:54,606 --> 00:15:57,064
that the shell does not
re-parse as commands.

226
00:15:57,404 --> 00:16:02,422
The mechanical rule is no expression inside
run at all; and env does not protect

227
00:16:02,462 --> 00:16:05,646
against eval or an unvalidated
write to GITHUB_ENV.

228
00:16:05,986 --> 00:16:11,213
A single-line scan misses multi-line scripts;
scan the lines inside each run block.

229
00:16:13,053 --> 00:16:16,583
Read section 21A.6 of Chapter 21A.

230
00:16:16,923 --> 00:16:21,873
Today you turned a line that looked
harmless into a finding, a fix and a review

231
00:16:21,913 --> 00:16:25,221
comment. Write that comment
once yourself in the lab.

232
00:16:25,261 --> 00:16:30,084
Next time: third-party actions, mutable
tags, commit pinning and organization

233
00:16:30,124 --> 00:16:34,000
policies. Until then, look at
the state first and type second.

234
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:35,516
See you in the next one.
